   "No external LED: the tutorial uses the built-in LED on pin 13, which is part of the Uno, so it is not a separate node.",
   "Potentiometer straddles the breadboard centre gap: outer legs in the bottom half (columns 10 and 12, row e), wiper leg in the top half of column 11. Hole positions are estimated from the image.",
   "Fix for V4: the pot wiper leg and the yellow wire previously both used 11t.g. They now use different holes of the same column-11 top strip: pot wiper in 11t.f, yellow wire in 11t.g. Both are electrically one node, so the connection is unchanged.",
   "Black wire goes to the second GND header pin in the image; modelled as GND.1 since the Uno's GND pins are the same node.",
   "Outer legs are symmetric, so GND/VCC assignment follows the wire colours (black on column 10, red on column 12).",
   "The schematic confirms the wiring: 5V to one pot end, GND to the other end, wiper to A0."
  ]
